title: Bloody March in Berlin
subtitle: The Berlin councils call a general strike.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 3 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-arrival: {!
RG.startStrike('berlin', true);
RG.district('berlin', {militancy: 10});
RG.news('Berlin councils call a general strike', 2);
!}

= Bloody March in Berlin

On 3 March the Berlin workers' councils called a general strike for the recognition of the councils and the release of political prisoners. The city stopped. In the east, around the Alexanderplatz, crowds plundered shops, and sailors of the People's Naval Division began handing out rifles.

Noske's troops are moving in. [? if luxemburg_alive = 1 : Luxemburg writes from hiding that the strike must not become a second January. ?][? if luxemburg_alive = 0 : Jogiches writes that the strike must not become a second January. ?] The young men of Lichtenberg are not listening.

- @unarmed: Back the strike, and keep out of the fighting.
- @rising: Join the sailors at the barricades.

@unarmed
subtitle: Some of our people will fight anyway.
on-arrival: march_line = 1; lean_luxemburgist += 2; district_berlin_members -= 0.3

On 5 March *Die Rote Fahne* tells the workers to stay off the streets. The paper is banned the next day.

- @terror: Continue...

@rising
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Noske has artillery, aircraft and orders to shoot. [? if liebknecht_alive = 1 : Liebknecht will not stay behind. ?]
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids an armed rising.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.march_line = 2;
Q.militancy += 8;
Q.district_berlin_members -= Q.e19_buried ? 0.4 : 0.8;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

For four days the east of Berlin is a battlefield. [? if e19_buried = 1 : The rifles buried in January come out of the allotment sheds, and the Lichtenberg men hold longer than anyone expected. ?]

- @terror: Continue...

@terror
title: Noske's Order
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.rote_fahne_banned = 1;
Q.freikorps_strength += 20;
if (Q.liebknecht_alive == 1 && Q.march_line == 2 && Math.random() < 0.4) {
    RG.kill('liebknecht', {news: 'Karl Liebknecht shot at a checkpoint in Lichtenberg', priority: 3});
    RG.ledger('Karl Liebknecht fell at the barricades of Lichtenberg in March 1919.', 'e19_lieb_march');
    Q.liebknecht_alive = 0;
    Q.liebknecht_advisor = 0;
    Q.liebknecht_march_death = 1;
}
RG.districtSync();
RG.endStrike('berlin', 'crushed');
RG.district('berlin', {repression: 15, guards: -0.5});
RG.news('Noske orders: anyone found armed to be shot', 3);
!}

= Noske's Order

On 9 March, after false reports that the rebels had massacred the police in Lichtenberg, Noske ordered that anyone found carrying arms against the government be shot on the spot. Twenty-nine sailors who came to collect their pay were shot in a courtyard in the Französische Strasse. About twelve hundred people are dead. [? if liebknecht_march_death = 1 : Karl Liebknecht was recognised at a checkpoint in Lichtenberg and shot. ?]

Leo Jogiches has spent two months finding the men who killed Luxemburg and Liebknecht. The police know where he sleeps.

- @leave: Order Jogiches to leave Berlin.
- @work: Let him finish his investigation.

@leave
subtitle: He has hidden from the Tsar's police for thirty years. He will probably get away.
on-arrival: {!
Q.jogiches_alive = Math.random() < 0.75 ? 1 : 0;
Q.e19_jogiches_report = 0;
!}
go-to: jogiches

@work
subtitle: The murderers will be named. Jogiches knows the risk, and so do we: it is worse than even.
on-arrival: {!
Q.jogiches_alive = Math.random() < 0.35 ? 1 : 0;
Q.e19_jogiches_report = 1;
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.spd_relation -= 4;
!}
go-to: jogiches

@jogiches
title: The Zentrale
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
if (!Q.jogiches_alive) {
    RG.kill('jogiches', {news: 'Leo Jogiches shot in Moabit "while trying to escape"', priority: 3});
    Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 5;
}
if (Q.luxemburg_alive) {
    Q.party_chair = 'Rosa Luxemburg';
    Q.levi_chair = 0;
} else if (Q.jogiches_alive) {
    Q.party_chair = 'Leo Jogiches';
    Q.levi_chair = 0;
} else {
    Q.party_chair = 'Paul Levi';
    Q.levi_chair = 1;
    RG.setRole('levi', 'Chair of the Zentrale');
    RG.news('Paul Levi takes over the Communist Zentrale', 2);
    RG.ledger('Paul Levi took over the Zentrale in March 1919.', 'e19_levi_chair');
}
!}

= The Zentrale

[? if jogiches_alive = 0 : On 10 March Jogiches is arrested in his flat in Neukölln and taken to the remand prison in Moabit. That evening a police sergeant shoots him in the back in a corridor. ?][? if jogiches_alive = 1 : The police come to Jogiches' flat in Neukölln on 10 March and find it empty. ?][? if jogiches_alive = 1 and e19_jogiches_report = 1 : His report on the Eden Hotel appears in the illegal *Rote Fahne* a week later, with the names of the officers. ?]

[? if levi_chair = 1 : The leadership passes to **Paul Levi**, a Frankfurt lawyer of thirty-five, Luxemburg's defender in court and her closest political friend. The Left Radicals detest him. ?][? if levi_chair = 0 and luxemburg_alive = 1 : **Rosa Luxemburg** still leads the Zentrale from hiding, with Paul Levi as her right hand. ?][? if levi_chair = 0 and luxemburg_alive = 0 : **Leo Jogiches** still holds the Zentrale together, with Paul Levi beside him. ?]
